BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] Current Events Discussion Group
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261009T113000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261009T123000
DTSTAMP:20260720T200937Z
UID:smcl-6a5a9bfec44ff5b82cf5e5f8@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Join us every second Friday of the month for a Current Events 
 Discussion group from August to November. Each month\, we will select an 
 article to read from publications like The Atlantic\, The New Yorker\, The
  Guardian\, The New York Times\, The Wall Street Journal\, and New York Ma
 gazine. You can access all these resources digitally with your library car
 d. \n\n\nQ&A \n\nQ: What if I don’t have a library card?  \n\nA: We can 
 help you get one. If you need support\, you can email atherton@smcl.org\, 
 or ask a friendly staff member.  \n\nQ: What if I don’t know how to acce
 ss magazines and newspapers online using my library card?  \n\nA: Our firs
 t session is December 12 at 11:30am\, and it will be an introduction to di
 scuss an overview of the discussion group and instructions on accessing th
 e articles. If you can’t make this session\, simply email atherton@smcl.
 org\, and we can setup an appointment to provide instructions.\n\nAges: Ad
 ult program (kids welcome to tag along\, not designed for them)\nRegistrat
 ion: required\nSource: https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a5a9bfec44ff
 5b82cf5e5f8\nLast synced: 2026-07-20 13:09 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a5a9bfec44ff5b82cf5e5f8
END:VEVENT
