BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] Fall in Love With the Classics at Holbrook Palmer Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260819T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260819T113000
DTSTAMP:20260720T200937Z
UID:smcl-6a02440a8e677a28001b57ab@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Join us this fall for a three-part classic literature discussi
 on series exploring love\, ambition\, and social expectations through unfo
 rgettable novels. We’ll meet monthly from August through November on the
  third Wednesday of the month for welcoming and engaging conversations. \n
 \n\nAt the first meeting\, we will introduce the structure of the series\,
  distribute the first book\, and give participants a chance to meet fellow
  readers before discussions begin.  Books will be provided. Attendance a
 t each discussion meeting is required in order to receive the next book in
  the series.\n\nOur first featured novel is Jane Austen’s Northanger Abb
 ey\, a witty and charming satire that follows young Catherine Morland as s
 he navigates friendship\, romance\, and imagination. Filled with humor and
  sharp social commentary\, Austen’s novel playfully examines the influen
 ce of gothic fiction and society’s expectations.\n\nThe book club will m
 eet at North Meadow Picnic Tables at Holbrook Palmer Park\n\nAges: Adult p
 rogram (kids welcome to tag along\, not designed for them)\nRegistration: 
 none\nSource: https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a02440a8e677a28001b57
 ab\nLast synced: 2026-07-20 13:09 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a02440a8e677a28001b57ab
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] Sketching with Sami
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260914T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260914T120000
DTSTAMP:20260720T200937Z
UID:smcl-6a481f6edd4fa0c68b5eb39e@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Come join Sami as we sketch the local plants in Holbrook-Palme
 r Park. Together\, we can learn more about what is blooming locally\, so t
 hat when we take walks outside in the future\, we will be able to recogniz
 e what is growing alongside us. Some techniques that will be taught by Sam
 i include how to sketch flowers and how to mix watercolors so that they ap
 pear more natural."\n\nSpace is limited\, and registration is required. Re
 gistrants will be emailed the exact location in Holbrook-Palmer Park.\n\nA
 ges: Adult program (kids welcome to tag along\, not designed for them)\nRe
 gistration: required\nSource: https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a481f
 6edd4fa0c68b5eb39e\nLast synced: 2026-07-20 13:09 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a481f6edd4fa0c68b5eb39e
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] Tai Chi
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260722T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260722T113000
DTSTAMP:20260720T200937Z
UID:smcl-6a345ef590cc4e3a790f2d9a@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Chen-style Taijiquan (Tai Chi) is widely acknowledged as the a
 ncestor of all other styles of Taijiquan. This class will introduce the Ch
 en-style Taijiquan form\, Silk-reeling Exercises and Wuji Qigong. The Chen
 -style Taijiquan form is soft and graceful with strong rooted stands that 
 will help students to develop strength\, balance\, coordination and an und
 erstanding of basic Taiji principles. Silk-reeling Exercises are a series 
 of spiral movements that promote muscle relaxation and flexibility by redu
 cing physical tension and strain. Wuji Qigong (standing meditation) will h
 elp students to cultivate internal energy (qi) with proper body alignment 
 for better internal energy flow\, which will enhance their immune systems 
 and reduce physical and mental stress.\n\nRegistration is encouraged but n
 ot required.\n\nAges: Adult program (kids welcome to tag along\, not desig
 ned for them)\nRegistration: required\nSource: https://smcl.bibliocommons.
 com/events/6a345ef590cc4e3a790f2d9a\nLast synced: 2026-07-20 13:09 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a345ef590cc4e3a790f2d9a
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] It's Sew Easy: Bucket Hat
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260726T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260726T140000
DTSTAMP:20260720T200937Z
UID:smcl-6a28878743b41b3d006d208a@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Interested in picking up the fun life skill of sewing? Our Sew
  Easy project for this month is Bucket Hat. Whether you're a beginner or e
 xperienced sewist\, this project is perfect for the summer. Get hands-on e
 xperience tracing a pattern\, flipping pieces inside out\, and topstitchin
 g.\n\nThis program is open only to adults 18+.\n\nSpace is limited\, so pl
 ease register at smcl.org/events  to reserve your spot. Sessions with the 
 same title are identical\, so please only sign up for one. We will start 
 letting participants in no earlier than the start time.\n\nAges: Adult pro
 gram (kids welcome to tag along\, not designed for them)\nRegistration: re
 quired\nSource: https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a28878743b41b3d006d
 208a\nLast synced: 2026-07-20 13:09 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a28878743b41b3d006d208a
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] Meet James Wang\, Author of What You Need to Know About AI\,
  in Conversation with Nydia Zhang
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260807T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260807T160000
DTSTAMP:20260720T200937Z
UID:smcl-6a513ae1e9de6536001ac257@local-events
DESCRIPTION:San Mateo County Libraries welcomes James Wang\, author of Wha
 t You Need to Know About AI\, for a timely and engaging conversation with 
 featured host Nydia Zhang.  \n\nArtificial intelligence is shaping the way
  we work\, learn\, create and connect. Whether you are new to AI or alread
 y following the latest developments\, this author talk offers a clear and 
 welcoming place to explore what AI is\, why it matters and how it may shap
 e our shared future.  \n\nA book signing will follow the talk. Free copies
  of What You Need to Know About AI will be available at the door\, while s
 upplies last. Giveaway copies are limited and offered on a first-come\, fi
 rst-served basis. \n\nAbout the Book \n\nIn What You Need to Know About AI
 \, James Wang cuts through the noise around one of today’s most talked-a
 bout technologies. With clarity and insight\, he explores the history\, pr
 inciples and real-world implications of AI\, helping readers better unders
 tand a fast-changing field that is already influencing daily life.  \n\nMe
 et James Wang \n\nJames Wang is a technologist\, investor and writer with 
 over a decade of experience in AI and deep tech. He is a general partner a
 t Creative Ventures\, an early-stage deep tech fund backing breakthroughs 
 in AI\, synthetic biology and advanced materials.  \n\nPreviously\, James 
 worked at Bridgewater Associates and worked at Google's "moonshot" innovat
 ion lab\, X. He has served as a board director at startups working in AI\,
  healthcare and robotics and is a regular guest lecturer at UC Berkeley on
  entrepreneurship and startup financing.  \n\nMeet Featured Host Nydia Zha
 ng \n\nNydia Zhang is an art gallerist\, Investor and social entrepreneur 
 whose work brings together art\, technology and social impart. She began h
 er career in Hong Kong’s gallery world before moving into venture capita
 l and private investments\, with a focus on food-tech and emerging technol
 ogies.  \n\nNydia co-founded a grant-making foundation for blockchain soci
 al impact initiatives and serves as an ambassador to the Global Blockchain
  Business Council\, a UN partner organization advancing technology for the
  Sustainable Development Goals. \n\nJoin us for an inspiring afternoon of
  learning\, connection and exploration as James Wang and Nydia Zhang help 
 make the world of AI feel more approachable\, relevant and connected to ou
 r everyday lives.\n\nAges: Adult program (kids welcome to tag along\, not 
 designed for them)\nRegistration: none\nSource: https://smcl.bibliocommons
 .com/events/6a513ae1e9de6536001ac257\nLast synced: 2026-07-20 13:09 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a513ae1e9de6536001ac257
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] Drop-In Sewing Machine Basics
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260802T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260802T140000
DTSTAMP:20260720T200937Z
UID:smcl-6a56951c17f387c203a51c09@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Interested in picking up the fun life skill of sewing? Not sur
 e how to get started? Our Drop-in Sewing Machine Basics session will be pe
 rfect for you! You’ll be guided on all the basics of using a Baby Lock J
 ubilant machine. From winding a bobbin\, threading the machine\, to runnin
 g some simple stitches. We’ll help you learn some best practices and gai
 n skills that you can use on future projects. No registration is required\
 , but sewing machines and space are limited. \n\nDrop-In Sewing Machine B
 asics is for adults 18 and older only. \n\nIf you are 6 to 18 years old\,
  you are welcome to register for Jr. Sewing\, which occurs every third Tue
 sday of the month.\n\nAges: Adult program (kids welcome to tag along\, not
  designed for them)\nRegistration: required\nSource: https://smcl.biblioco
 mmons.com/events/6a56951c17f387c203a51c09\nLast synced: 2026-07-20 13:09 P
 DT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a56951c17f387c203a51c09
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] Financial Wellness Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260910T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260910T193000
DTSTAMP:20260720T200937Z
UID:smcl-6a29f9ab16554cd59fc7e57a@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Join the Financial Wellness Book Club hosted by Atherton Libra
 ry and the San Mateo County Commission on the Status of Women. This summer
 \, we’re reading Make Money Move by Lauren Simmons and inviting communit
 y members to reflect on financial wellness\, confidence\, and healthier mo
 ney habits before gathering for a welcoming community conversation on Sept
 ember 10\, 6:00 PM - 7:30 PM. Together\, we hope to build a supportive spa
 ce where everyone feels encouraged to learn\, reflect\, and share perspect
 ives. Please join us!\n\nAges: Adult program (kids welcome to tag along\, 
 not designed for them)\nRegistration: required\nSource: https://smcl.bibli
 ocommons.com/events/6a29f9ab16554cd59fc7e57a\nLast synced: 2026-07-20 13:0
 9 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a29f9ab16554cd59fc7e57a
END:VEVENT
