BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] Lecture and Art Walk With Landscape and Muralist Painter Ann
  Elizabeth Thiermann - MFA
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260729T113000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260729T124500
DTSTAMP:20260720T200937Z
UID:smcl-6a29f9168d1b82ca9f790d14@local-events
DESCRIPTION:In partnership with the Atherton Arts Foundation\, join the At
 herton Library as we welcome Landscape and Muralist Painter Ann Elizabeth 
 Thiermann for a lecture and art walk. The program will feature a slidesh
 ow of 25 working artists' portraits and a tour with the artist of her Athe
 rton Town Hall exhibition. As an experienced college educator\, now Cabri
 llo College Emeritus\, her talks are engaging\, educational\, and fun. \
 n\nRegistration is encouraged but not required. \n\nAnn's work will be di
 splayed in the Atherton Town Hall in a Solo Exhibition through the end of 
 August. The subject of the exhibition is Portraits of Bay Area Women Arti
 sts Creating\, and Bay Area Trees: Orchards to Forests\, Woodlands to Sh
 ore.  \n\nAbout Ann:\n\nAnn Thiermann\, a classically-trained landscape 
 and figurative painter is the chosen winner of the 2027 Santa Cruz Arts Co
 mmission Artist of the Year Award. She has designed over seventy Californi
 a murals for sites which include: Oakland Museum\, Los Altos History Museu
 m\, CA Academy of Sciences\, Santa Cruz Museum of Natural History\, and U
 CSC. She is known for her California historical and Native American murals
  giving voice to Native American tribal traditions.\n\nAges: Adult program
  (kids welcome to tag along\, not designed for them)\nRegistration: requir
 ed\nSource: https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a29f9168d1b82ca9f790d14
 \nLast synced: 2026-07-20 13:09 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a29f9168d1b82ca9f790d14
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] Watercolor Painting in the Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260817T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260817T120000
DTSTAMP:20260720T200937Z
UID:smcl-6a5547510d65ac36003f7af3@local-events
DESCRIPTION:In this workshop\, we will explore the historical buildings an
 d diversity of trees in Holbrook Palmer Park\, and learn to make field ske
 tches in watercolor\, identify a picture frame in the field\, and construc
 t a quick composition with focal point\, contrast\, light\, and shadow. So
 me experience with drawing and painting is helpful.\n\nWe will meet in the
  first parking lot of Holbrook-Palmer Park. Registration is required\, and
  space is limited. \n\nThe library will provide some basic supplies. If y
 ou do plan to bring your own\, here is what the instructor recommends:\nsk
 etchbook with watercolor paper\nwatercolor travel kit and brushes\na small
  portable water container\nfolding stool or camping chair\nRegistration wi
 ll open on Monday\, July 13 @ 10:00 am. Please note that you will need to
  register for each individual session.\n\nAges: Adult program (kids welcom
 e to tag along\, not designed for them)\nRegistration: required\nSource: h
 ttps://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a5547510d65ac36003f7af3\nLast synced
 : 2026-07-20 13:09 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a5547510d65ac36003f7af3
END:VEVENT
