BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] Fall in Love with the Classics at Holbrook Palmer Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260916T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260916T113000
DTSTAMP:20260720T200937Z
UID:smcl-6a04d30fc7d3cd580058ff4d@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Join this fall for a three-part book discussion series explori
 ng \nlove\, ambition\, and social expectations through classic literature.
  This\n limited-run series invites readers to examine how relationships an
 d \nclass shape personal choices.\n\nWe’ll meet monthly from August thro
 ugh November on the third Wednesday of the month for welcoming and engagin
 g conversations. Books will be provided. Attendance at each discussion mee
 ting is required in order to receive the next book in the series.\n\nJoin 
 us for our discussion of Jane Austen's Northanger Abbey. Together we’ll
  explore the novel’s playful satire of gothic literature\, its sharp obs
 ervations on society and reading culture\, and the charming\, often comica
 l journey of Catherine Morland as she navigates friendship\, imagination\,
  and first love.\n\nDuring this meeting\, participants will receive our ne
 xt featured novel\, Elizabeth Gaskell's North and South. A powerful explo
 ration of class tension\, industrialization\, and shifting social values\,
  the novel follows Margaret Hale as she confronts the contrasts between En
 gland’s rural South and the bustling\, conflict-laden North\, along wit
 h the complex and evolving relationship she forms with mill owner John Tho
 rnton.\n\nThe book club will meet at the North Meadow Picnic Tables at Hol
 brook Palmer Park.\n\nAges: Adult program (kids welcome to tag along\, not
  designed for them)\nRegistration: none\nSource: https://smcl.bibliocommon
 s.com/events/6a04d30fc7d3cd580058ff4d\nLast synced: 2026-07-20 13:09 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a04d30fc7d3cd580058ff4d
END:VEVENT
